# awcms-astro — build-time configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Everything here is read at BUILD time; nothing in
# this file reaches the browser. Astro only inlines variables prefixed
# `PUBLIC_`, and none of these are — do not add a `PUBLIC_` alias for the token.

# --- Site identity -----------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical absolute origin. Canonical links, hreflang alternates, Open
# Graph URLs, robots.txt, and the sitemap are all built from it. A wrong value
# does not fail the build; it publishes a site pointing every crawler elsewhere.
SITE_URL=https://example.com
SITE_NAME=Example Site
SITE_DESCRIPTION=Public information site built on the awcms-astro template.

# Locale prefixes OTHER than the default locale, comma separated. Must match
# `localeMeta` in src/config/site.ts — astro.config.mjs cannot import that file
# (it runs first), so the two are kept in step by hand.
SITE_LOCALES=en

# --- awcms content backend ---------------------------------------------------
# Origin of the awcms instance. No trailing slash needed; one is stripped.
AWCMS_API_URL=https://cms.example.com

# A BUILD-TIME, READ-ONLY token. It reads published content while `astro build`
# runs and is never emitted into the output. If this token can write, or can
# read another tenant's data, the mistake is on the awcms side — issue it with
# the narrowest role that can list published posts and nothing else.
AWCMS_API_TOKEN=replace-me

# --- Tenant resolution -------------------------------------------------------
# An awcms instance is multi-tenant; this site is one tenant. The chain is tried
# in order and the build FAILS if none is set — see src/lib/awcms/tenant.ts for
# why guessing is not an option here.
#
#   1. AWCMS_TENANT_CODE          — explicit tenant code. Prefer this.
#   2. AWCMS_TENANT_ID            — explicit tenant UUID.
#   3. AWCMS_DEFAULT_TENANT_CODE  — the fallback when this site names no tenant.
#
# Pin these PER ENVIRONMENT. Leaving the first two unset and relying on the
# default is supported and is exactly what the fallback is for — but it makes
# "which tenant does this site publish?" an answer buried in someone else's
# configuration rather than a stated one.
AWCMS_TENANT_CODE=
# AWCMS_TENANT_ID=
AWCMS_DEFAULT_TENANT_CODE=default
